1
00:00:00,091 --> 00:00:04,791
Which site was that? — The question a second location adds to every report.

2
00:00:09,124 --> 00:00:12,344
Every place this practice works, in one list.

3
00:00:12,344 --> 00:00:17,140
Two clinics, a community hall, and a van.

4
00:00:17,140 --> 00:00:21,135
The hall is not the practice’s building. It is still a site.

5
00:00:21,135 --> 00:00:27,209
Which is why a camp points at one, instead of keeping its own address.

6
00:00:27,209 --> 00:00:31,858
One site is primary. Anything not assigned to a site belongs to it.

7
00:00:31,858 --> 00:00:35,781
So nothing is ever stranded while the second site is being set up.

8
00:00:35,846 --> 00:00:41,906
A second site, not a second system. — Clinics, halls and vans — all the same kind of thing.
